The agent is deliberately the permissive half. It is the only component that
runs inside a customer's cluster, so a SecOps team has to be able to read it,
audit it, build it themselves and vendor it into their own tooling without the
copyleft obligation reaching their infrastructure. The server and console —
where the product is — are AGPL: running a modified KubeMG as a network service
means offering that modified source to its users.

